# devenv-attach hosts config — copy to ~/.config/devenv/hosts.conf
#
# Flat KEY=VALUE pairs, sourced by Bash. For each container name `foo`, define
# FOO_HOST and FOO_PORT. The name argument to `devenv-attach` is uppercased
# (and hyphens become underscores) before lookup, so `devenv-attach acme`
# reads ACME_HOST + ACME_PORT, and `devenv-attach my-box` reads MY_BOX_HOST +
# MY_BOX_PORT.
#
# This file is sourced — keep it to plain shell-assignable scalars. No spaces
# around `=`, no expansions you don't intend to be evaluated.
#
# Recommended permissions: chmod 0600 ~/.config/devenv/hosts.conf

# One VPS, two containers on different ports:
ACME_HOST=vps1.example.com
ACME_PORT=2231

BLOG_HOST=vps1.example.com
BLOG_PORT=2247

# A second VPS, one container:
SCRATCH_HOST=vps2.example.com
SCRATCH_PORT=2200
